{
  "_comment": [
    "The register of every check this repository owns, and of every file under tools/ that is",
    "not one. It exists because the release gate went green for five rounds over a check that",
    "was failing: tests/unit/rooms/prop_frame_capture exits 2 on the default theme and nothing",
    "in the repository ever ran it. A check nobody runs is worse than no check, because it",
    "reads as coverage.",
    "",
    "This file says what a check IS. It never says how a check WENT: that is the results",
    "ledger, reports/checks/<id>.json, written by tools/run-checks.sh out of the exit code the",
    "process actually returned. The register used to carry a known_failing string somebody",
    "typed, and the gate's colour was a function of that field - which is the same disease one",
    "level up: a claim standing in for a result. It is gone; nothing here can make a check look",
    "green or red.",
    "",
    "Three things read this file:",
    "  tools/run-checks.sh          runs a tier of it, records what happened, and is what CI calls",
    "  tools/checks.py              parses it, and reads and writes the ledger",
    "  tests/unit/tools/check_registry_test.gd   is in the gate and fails when",
    "    - a file under tools/ or a capture scene under tests/ is not declared here,",
    "    - a declared check names a command that does not exist,",
    "    - a check with \"runs\": \"ci\" is not referenced by .github/workflows/ci.yml,",
    "    - a check with \"runs\": \"manual\" has no \"why_manual\" saying what runs it instead,",
    "    - a check declares a status of its own instead of leaving that to the ledger,",
    "    - or a check outside tier 1 has no recent passing record in the ledger.",
    "",
    "That last rule is the point of the whole file now. The gate is tier 1, and tier 1 is one",
    "invocation of the 48 this register holds; the other 47 are captures, soaks and packaging",
    "steps that a green gate used to say nothing at all about. It says something about them",
    "now, and the only way to make it say so is to run them."
  ],
  "schema": {
    "id": "unique name, also the argument to tools/run-checks.sh",
    "title": "what the check answers",
    "tier": "cheap | unit | rendered | soak | package | vm",
    "command": "argv prefix, relative to the project root",
    "matrix": "list of argv suffixes; the command runs once per row (default: one empty row)",
    "env": "environment the check needs",
    "runs": "ci (referenced by .github/workflows/ci.yml) | manual (needs why_manual)",
    "asserts": "true when the check fails on its own; false when it only produces pictures for a human",
    "outputs": "files under tests/out/ the check must leave behind, %s replaced by the theme suffix",
    "subjects": "for the scenarios check: TestScenarios.SUBJECTS, pinned so neither list can shrink quietly",
    "screens": "for the gallery check: UiGallery.SCREENS, pinned the same way"
  },
  "policy": {
    "_comment": [
      "Where results are recorded and how old one may be before the gate stops believing it.",
      "Both are bounded by constants in tests/unit/tools/check_registry_test.gd, so widening the",
      "window here does not widen it in the gate: a max age over the ceiling fails the suite."
    ],
    "results_dir": "reports/checks",
    "result_max_age_hours": 48
  },
