      "asserts": true
    },
    {
      "id": "appimage",
      "title": "the AppImage variant builds",
      "tier": "package",
      "command": [
        "tools/appimage.sh"
      ],
      "runs": "manual",
      "asserts": true,
      "why_manual": [
        "It downloads appimagetool from the network at build time into ~/.cache, which makes",
        "the step fail for a reason that is not this project. The .deb is the artefact the",
        "shipped package is, and it is what CI builds and unpacks; the AppImage shares the",
        "same tools/export.sh output, so a broken export fails the packages job first.",
        "Run it by hand before an AppImage release."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omarchy-vm",
      "title": "tier 3: the packaged .deb on a genuine Omarchy desktop, and the live retint proof",
      "tier": "vm",
      "command": [
        "tools/vm/verify.sh"
      ],
      "runs": "manual",
      "asserts": true,
      "why_manual": [
        "It needs /dev/kvm, ~6 GB of Omarchy ISO and about ten minutes of unattended install.",
        "No hosted runner offers nested virtualisation, so this cannot be a CI job; it is run",
        "by hand on a machine with KVM before a release (docs/TESTING.md tier 3), and its",
        "output is tests/out/vm/verify.txt plus one PNG per theme switch."
      ]
    }
